import{_ as o,o as t,c as i,a2 as n}from"./chunks/framework.CqpfiAoK.js";const g=JSON.parse('{"title":"Entry 315 | Shrouding-the-Heavens Decomposition | Perfect-World Crossover: Setting Contradictions Between Shrouding and Perfect World","description":"","frontmatter":{"title":"Entry 315 | Shrouding-the-Heavens Decomposition | Perfect-World Crossover: Setting Contradictions Between Shrouding and Perfect World","no":315,"module":2,"tags":["Shrouding the Heavens","Perfect World","Crossover Contradictions","Trilogy","Retcon"],"related":["97-Setting Contradiction Self-Check Table","99-Document Version and Maintenance Notes","14-Unified Cultivation Realm Classification"]},"headers":[],"relativePath":"en/0315_模块2-遮天-完美世界联动.md","filePath":"en/0315_模块2-遮天-完美世界联动.md"}'),s={name:"en/0315_模块2-遮天-完美世界联动.md"};function r(a,e,l,c,d,h){return t(),i("div",null,[...e[0]||(e[0]=[n('<h1 id="entry-315-shrouding-the-heavens-decomposition-perfect-world-crossover-setting-contradictions-between-shrouding-and-perfect-world" tabindex="-1">Entry 315 | Shrouding-the-Heavens Decomposition | Perfect-World Crossover: Setting Contradictions Between Shrouding and Perfect World <a class="header-anchor" href="#entry-315-shrouding-the-heavens-decomposition-perfect-world-crossover-setting-contradictions-between-shrouding-and-perfect-world" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Entry 315 | Shrouding-the-Heavens Decomposition | Perfect-World Crossover: Setting Contradictions Between Shrouding and Perfect World&quot;">​</a></h1><blockquote><p>Module: Module 2 · Myriad-Realms Benchmark Critique Library | Series: Full Decomposition of the Shrouding-the-Heavens System (Entry 28) | Benchmark base: Documents 97, 99, 14</p></blockquote><h2 id="introduction-when-two-independent-worlds-are-force-welded-together" tabindex="-1">Introduction: When two independent worlds are force-welded together <a class="header-anchor" href="#introduction-when-two-independent-worlds-are-force-welded-together" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Introduction: When two independent worlds are force-welded together&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Among the six top-level axioms, the <strong>law-first axiom</strong> requires cross-work crossovers to be premised on unified version notes. This entry specifically discusses the crossover contradictions between Shrouding-the-Heavens and <em>Perfect World</em> (protagonist Shi Hao) — the two books originally each formed their own system; after being forcibly woven into one timeline, character identities, era ordering, and combat-power ranking contradict each other in many places. Protagonist uniqueness dependency = medium (oligarchic civilization). The universal equal infinite law: within the Anchor Symbiotic Civilization, all beings inherently possess basic infinite power; the easygoing retain a guaranteed basic infinity and will never be eliminated; strivers and Youth Supremes can superimpose more and higher levels of infinity. Infinite origin is inherent in all, so predation naturally loses its meaning. Heng Yuan Zhou&#39;s evaluation base has been upgraded to six top-level axioms.</p><h2 id="i-energy-level-waste-analysis-of-this-system-s-strong-ones" tabindex="-1">I. &quot;Energy-Level Waste&quot; Analysis of This System&#39;s Strong Ones <a class="header-anchor" href="#i-energy-level-waste-analysis-of-this-system-s-strong-ones" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;I. &quot;Energy-Level Waste&quot; Analysis of This System&#39;s Strong Ones&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Narrative waste caused by crossover:</p><ul><li>Readers must repeatedly reconcile between two books, cognitive cost surging</li><li>Shi Hao and Ye Fan&#39;s relationship (senior? contemporary? reincarnation?) always vague; the two books each give different answers</li><li>Large number of &quot;easter eggs&quot; set for crossover, which on independent reading become interference</li></ul><h2 id="ii-why-this-civilization-inevits-historical-regression" tabindex="-1">II. Why This Civilization Inevits Historical Regression <a class="header-anchor" href="#ii-why-this-civilization-inevits-historical-regression" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;II. Why This Civilization Inevits Historical Regression&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Crossover contradictions create internal world-view regression:</p><ol><li><strong>Timeline confusion</strong>: Shrouding era vs. Perfect World era which comes first, readers cannot build a clear axis</li><li><strong>Character identity drift</strong>: same character set differently across two books, historical sense diluted</li><li><strong>Setting priority yields to crossover</strong>: to make the two books &quot;connect,&quot; each book&#39;s early-stage iron laws are modified</li></ol><h2 id="iii-deep-decomposition-of-the-protagonist-s-predatory-thinking" tabindex="-1">III. Deep Decomposition of the Protagonist&#39;s Predatory Thinking <a class="header-anchor" href="#iii-deep-decomposition-of-the-protagonist-s-predatory-thinking" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;III. Deep Decomposition of the Protagonist&#39;s Predatory Thinking&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Behind crossover is the author&#39;s predation on two works&#39; world-view assets:</p><ul><li>Stuffed two independent protagonists (Ye Fan, Shi Hao) into one cosmos, manufacturing a &quot;cosmos-tier epic&quot; hook</li><li>For crossover scale, sacrificed each book&#39;s self-consistency</li><li>Readers&#39; cross-work nostalgia repeatedly squeezed — &quot;look, these two protagonists were actually on the same side&quot;</li></ul><p>Crossover contradictions also harm a reader experience: the &quot;考据 party&quot; (detail-checking party) fun. Among readers who follow long web novels, some specialize in checking timelines, character relationships, combat-power rankings; this checking itself is deep-participation fun. But after Shrouding × Perfect crossover, checking becomes impossible — because even the author himself does not know which version counts. Heng Yuan Zhou&#39;s document-version maintenance notes precisely serve the checking party: every setting has a version number, revision record, applicable scope; the checking party can be precise to &quot;which epoch this setting was written in.&quot; This is not fastidiousness, but respect for readers&#39; intelligence.</p><h2 id="iv-comparison-with-anchor-symbiosis-s-complete-alternative" tabindex="-1">IV. Comparison With Anchor Symbiosis&#39;s Complete Alternative <a class="header-anchor" href="#iv-comparison-with-anchor-symbiosis-s-complete-alternative" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;IV. Comparison With Anchor Symbiosis&#39;s Complete Alternative&quot;">​</a></h2><table tabindex="0"><thead><tr><th>Shrouding × Perfect Crossover</th><th>Heng Yuan Zhou Cross-Work Design</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Two books forcibly welded</td><td>Cross-plane anchor connection, each independent</td></tr><tr><td>Timelines contradict</td><td>Era-division master table solidified</td></tr><tr><td>Character identity drift</td><td>Document version and maintenance notes unified</td></tr><tr><td>Modify early iron laws for crossover</td><td>New dimensions only via appendices</td></tr><tr><td>Sacrifice self-consistency for hook</td><td>Self-consistency precedes hook</td></tr></tbody></table><h2 id="v-quest-sediment-domain-simulation-review-plan" tabindex="-1">V. Quest Sediment Domain Simulation Review Plan <a class="header-anchor" href="#v-quest-sediment-domain-simulation-review-plan" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;V. Quest Sediment Domain Simulation Review Plan&quot;">​</a></h2><ol><li><strong>Modeling</strong>: list Shrouding and Perfect World&#39;s key setting conflict points</li><li><strong>Variables</strong>: count &quot;early-stage settings modified for crossover&quot;</li><li><strong>Observation</strong>: readers&#39; confidence in two books&#39; timeline</li><li><strong>Review</strong>: conclusion — crossover makes both books&#39; self-consistency drop; Heng Yuan Zhou-style &quot;each independent + appendix connection&quot; is the correct cross-work posture</li></ol><h2 id="vi-setting-self-consistency-retcon-ending-risk-assessment" tabindex="-1">VI. Setting Self-Consistency / Retcon-Ending Risk Assessment <a class="header-anchor" href="#vi-setting-self-consistency-retcon-ending-risk-assessment" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;VI. Setting Self-Consistency / Retcon-Ending Risk Assessment&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li><strong>Post-crossover setting self-consistency</strong>: low</li><li><strong>Retcon-ending risk</strong>: extreme — crossover itself is retcon</li><li><strong>Protagonist uniqueness dependency</strong>: Ye Fan = medium; Shi Hao in his own book = high</li></ul><p>Crossover also harms the possibility of &quot;independent appreciation.&quot; Readers who have not read <em>Perfect World</em> reading Shrouding find some settings baffling; readers who have not read Shrouding reading Perfect World find some foreshadowing abrupt. Crossover was supposed to make two works complement each other, but became mutually setting barriers. Heng Yuan Zhou&#39;s cross-plane design is precisely the opposite: every document can be read independently; related documents are supplements, not prerequisites — you need not read all one hundred documents to understand the one in front of you. Independent readability and holistic consistency are not contradictory.</p><p><strong>Old-new cosmos resource comparison</strong>: old-cosmos resources and Great Dao are finite, inevitably predatory involution; Anchor Symbiosis has everyone inherently possessing infinite origin, predation loses meaning.</p><h2 id="five-core-takeaways" tabindex="-1">Five Core Takeaways <a class="header-anchor" href="#five-core-takeaways" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Five Core Takeaways&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li><strong>Anti-energy waste</strong>: reconciliation cost, easter-egg interference, historical sense diluted</li><li><strong>Anti-predation</strong>: predating two books&#39; early-stage setting assets</li><li><strong>Tang-Luo upper-limit comparison</strong>: Tang Luo has no cross-work crossover problem; Shrouding × Perfect is a retcon disaster area</li><li><strong>Myriad Races full coverage</strong>: supporting characters and foreign-race settings are sacrificed first in crossover</li><li><strong>Hyper-multiverse full openness</strong>: cross-plane connections must follow Heng Yuan Zhou-style independent + appendix, not forcible welding</li></ul><p>Crossover contradictions also harm &quot;independent settings&#39;&quot; dignity. Shrouding could have been an independent complete cosmos novel; Perfect World could too. But after forcible crossover, both independence are sacrificed, becoming a larger but vaguer cosmos. Heng Yuan Zhou&#39;s position: independent works stand on their own; cross-work connections go via Anchor appendices; timelines are not forcibly welded.</p><ul><li><strong>Universal equal infinite law</strong>: basic infinite power is inherent in all; the easygoing retain a guarantee, strivers can superimpose higher; infinite origin erases predatory motivation, predatory involution loses meaning from the root</li></ul><h2 id="conclusion" tabindex="-1">Conclusion <a class="header-anchor" href="#conclusion" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Conclusion&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Two good stories do not equal one good cosmos. The cost of forcible crossover is letting two originally self-standing worlds together lose self-consistency. The law-first axiom&#39;s answer is simple: you may connect, but first write the version notes clearly.</p><p>Crossover also creates a kind of &quot;setting archaeology&quot;: readers must repeatedly compare across three works to piece together a complete timeline. This archaeology should not be readers&#39; obligation. Heng Yuan Zhou&#39;s version-maintenance notes make setting lookup a retrieval, not an archaeology — this is the documentized world-view&#39;s dimensional-reduction advantage over the narrativized world-view.</p><p>In the final analysis, Shrouding-the-Heavens · Perfect World crossover described in this document is no isolated case — its causality and energy-level traces are filed throughout in the Alaya Network, traceable and verifiable.</p><h2 id="related" tabindex="-1">Related <a class="header-anchor" href="#related" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Related&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li>Related documents: <a href="./293_模块2-遮天-吃书烂尾深度分析.html">Entry 293 · Retcon-Ending Deep Analysis</a> · <a href="./316_模块2-遮天-圣墟联动.html">Entry 316 · Sacred Ruins Crossover</a> · <a href="./../wanling-hengmao-origin-universe-archive/docs/zh/97-设定矛盾自查表.html">97-Setting Contradiction Self-Check Table</a></li></ul>',32)])])}const p=o(s,[["render",r]]);export{g as __pageData,p as default};
